  "cards": [
    { "dot": "cyan", "title": "Pipeline, in order", "items": [
      "llmAdminDoor → requestContext (request id, real visitor IP) → evalPass",
      "helmet → CORS → JSON body ≤ 100 kb",
      "/api: rate limit 300 per 15 min → authenticate (JWT + session, diagram 03)",
      "Per route: csrfGuard on cookie routes → tighter limit → requirePermission → validate (zod) → Idempotency-Key on bookings",
      "No match → notFound; any error → errorHandler, one JSON shape { error, message }"
    ] },
    { "dot": "rose", "title": "Who may enter", "items": [
      "401 = we don't know you (sign in); 403 = we know you, and you may not",
      "Routes ask for a permission ('patients.write'), never a role",
      "auth/permissions.js lists each role's permissions: patient, viewer, staff, owner",
      "A temporary password opens only the change-password route"
    ] },
    { "dot": "emerald", "title": "Controller → service → model", "items": [
      "Controller: read req.valid → call one service → send JSON (views/ shape it)",
      "Service: the clinic's rules (who owns what, what may change)",
      "Model: one table or one database function, errors thrown by unwrap()"
    ] },
    { "dot": "amber", "title": "Database side", "items": [
      "Every query uses the service role: Postgres has no other door",
      "Callers with pii.read get the plain view, everyone else the _masked twin",
      "Writes send x-actor-id and x-change-via, so the audit log knows who did it",
      "Knowledge files go to Supabase Storage straight from knowledgeService"
    ] },
    { "dot": "slate", "title": "Rate limits per IP", "items": [
      "sign-in 10 · codes 5 · refresh 120 per 15 min",
      "bookings 20 per hour · chat 20 per minute",
      "The agent evals (x-eval-key) skip these limits"
    ] }
  ]
